{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/elcbq9kj","slide":1,"name":"conclusions","text":"1. Morphology-aware GMR improves reference fidelity and structural feasibility.\n2. Stable execution depends on informative reward gradients and coherent whole-body objectives.\n3. Pretraining and temporal context help only when their representation matches the target task and optimiser.","textPreview":"1. Morphology-aware GMR improves reference fidelity and structural feasibility. | 2. Stable execution depends on informative reward gradi...","textChars":286,"textLines":3,"bbox":[1205,2302,940,205]}
